<!--
    Icelandic (is) UI locale. Glossary fixed BEFORE translating; every string
    below follows it. Biblical vocabulary in the register of the Icelandic
    Bible Society's Biblían (2007).

      verse ............... vers (n., pl. vers)
      chapter ............. kafli (pl. kaflar)
      Old Testament ....... Gamla testamentið
      New Testament ....... Nýja testamentið
      Apocrypha ........... Apókrýfar bækur
      Gospel (a book) ..... guðspjall (pl. guðspjöllin)
      the Good News ....... Fagnaðarerindið
      apostle ............. postuli
      Acts ................ Postulasagan
      epistles ............ bréfin (postulabréfin)
      Psalms / Psalter .... Sálmarnir / Saltarinn
      Proverbs ............ Orðskviðirnir
      prophets ............ spámennirnir
      Scripture ........... Ritningin
      salvation ........... hjálpræði
      words of Christ ..... orð Krists
      Holy Spirit ......... Heilagur andi
      Strong's numbers .... Strong-númer
      concordance ......... samhljóðun
      cross-references .... millivísanir
      translation ......... þýðing
      reading plan ........ lestraráætlun
      bookmark ............ bókamerki
      note ................ athugasemd
      highlight ........... áherslulitur
      side by side ........ hlið við hlið (samhliða)
      narration ........... upplestur
      text-to-speech ...... talgervill
      speech engine ....... talgervill
      sleep timer ......... svefnteljari
      widget .............. græja
      offline ............. án nettengingar
      download ............ sækja / niðurhal
      backup .............. öryggisafrit
      settings ............ stillingar
      grammar terms ....... native Icelandic school grammar where one exists
                            (nafnorð, sögn, nútíð, germynd, framsöguháttur,
                            nefnifall ...); Hebrew-specific categories keep
                            their Latin names as in the other locales
                            (status constructus, qal, niphal ...).
    Product names stay as is: Hexapla, KJV, Strong, Webster, Literata, Junicode.
-->
